---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 9, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Cookie Policy for CodesCompiler explaining essential, analytics, preference, and advertising cookies."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-white shadow-sm my-8 rounded-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8"><strong>Last Updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-brand prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p>
        This Cookie Policy explains how CodesCompiler uses cookies and similar technologies
        on <strong>codescompiler.com</strong> and <strong>app.codescompiler.com</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files stored on your device by a website. They can help a
        website remember preferences, provide functionality, understand traffic, and support
        advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Types of Cookies We May Use</h2>
      <h3>Essential Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        These may be needed for basic website functions, security, navigation, preferences,
        and features such as theme selection.
      </p>

      <h3>Analytics Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        We may use analytics technologies, including Google Analytics, to understand website
        traffic and improve our tutorials, tools, and user experience.
      </p>

      <h3>Advertising Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        Where Google AdSense or other advertising services are enabled, advertising providers
        may use cookies and similar technologies to deliver, measure, personalize, or limit
        advertisements.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Managing Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        You can usually control or delete cookies through your browser settings. You can also
        review Google's advertising privacy choices through
        <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google My Ad Center</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Some cookies may be set by third-party services embedded in or linked from the
        website. Their use of cookies is governed by their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Cookie Policy when our technologies, advertising providers, or
        legal requirements change. The latest version will always be published on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about cookies can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:contact@codescompiler.com">contact@codescompiler.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
